--- !u!114 &1332317225077263
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1167556175868004}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 396459964a4a45a4b7cef4c9082df875, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPC
  displayName: "The Phantom"
  title: "The Opera Ghost, master of the cellars"
  tint: {r: 0.25, g: 0.08, b: 0.3, a: 1}
  dialogue: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 59e9fb6e424341bc82bf4ce35f480039, type: 3}
  lines:
  - text: "What have you done with my bag? So it was to take my bag that you asked me to release you!"
  - text: "Oh, yes, the heat is unendurable!"
  - text: "Why do you shake me like that? I tell you that I am going to die... Yes, I kissed her alive ..."
  - text: "Yes, she was waiting for me ... waiting for me erect and alive, a real, living bride ... as she hoped to be saved ... And, when I ... came forward, more timid than ..."
  - text: "a little child, she did not run away ... no, no ... she stayed ... she waited for me ... I even believe ... daroga ... that she put out her forehead ... a little ..."
  - text: "oh, not much ... just a little ... like a living bride ... And ... and ... I ... kissed her! ... I! ... I! ... I! ... And she did not die! ..."
  - text: "She used to run away ... and throw me my mask! ... Nor any other woman ... ever, ever! ... Ah, you can understand, my happiness was so great, I cried."
  - text: "And I fell at her feet, crying ... and I kissed her feet ... her little feet ... crying. You're crying, too, daroga ... and she cried also ... the angel cried! ..."
  - text: "I went and released the young man, and told him to come with me to Christine ... They kissed before me in the Louis-Philippe room ... Christine had my ring ..."
  - text: "... I told her where she would find my body and what to do with it..."
  - text: "Then Christine kissed me, for the first time, herself, here, on the forehead--don't look, daroga!--here, on the forehead ..."
  - text: "Daroga, daroga, if Christine keeps her promise, she will come back soon! ..."
